#
# Drags drawn where the finger will be, not where it was.
#
# Patch 0016's resampling shows the finger where it was a resampling
# latency ago (16-40 ms, as reports arrive late and in bursts), and the
# frame reaches the glass about a period after its tick: on the Jolla Phone
# the page trailed the finger by 28-36 ms, felt as a drag that lags and a
# fling that starts late. As iOS and Android do, the page is now drawn
# ahead by the finger's recent velocity times that latency (plus 8 ms,
# PACIFIC_SCROLL_PREDICT_MS), extrapolating the smooth resampled position.
# The offset grows by at most 15% of a frame's own movement
# (PACIFIC_SCROLL_PREDICT_RAMP), so a drag starts without a lurch; it
# never moves the page against the finger, fades at low speed and when
# reports stop, is dropped on a reversal and eases back while the finger
# rests; the fling goes on from where the page is shown. PACIFIC_SCROLL_PREDICT=0 turns it off.
#
# 200 ms flicks at 1.4 css px/ms, the page's lag behind the finger over
# the last frames before the lift: 33-42 ms -> 2-12 ms. Steps while
# dragging stay as even as without it (13-22 px a frame at 90 Hz).
#
